  "id": "COMPOUND:14486 - PROTEIN:6231",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that memantine may interact with Histone-lysine N-methyltransferase, H3 lysine-9 specific 5 through a series of molecular targets. Memantine is known to target the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, which is a key component of the polycomb repressive complex 2 (PRC2) and is involved in histone methylation, particularly on lysine 9 of histone H3. This complex plays a critical role in gene regulation and is a target of several compounds, including (+)-Phylliroside, quillaic acid, and Dimethyl 3-hydroxyphthalate. These compounds are all capable of modulating the activity of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, which in turn affects the methylation of histone H3 lysine 9. The shared target of these compounds with the enzyme suggests a potential mechanism by which memantine could influence the activity of this enzyme. The evidence is consistent and supports a pathway where memantine indirectly affects the enzyme through its interaction with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, highlighting a possible role in modulating gene expression through histone modification.",
